    {
      "id": "O1",
      "revision": 1,
      "kind": "postcondition",
      "role": "guarantee",
      "required": true,
      "statement": "For every input satisfying A1, execution of the arity-1 typed entry solve in canonical program.vscore.json returns the exact integer sum Σ_{i=0}^{n-1} floor((a*i+b)/m). Each floor is the unique integer q satisfying q*m <= a*i+b < (q+1)*m, including negative numerators; n=0 yields zero. Universal refinement must relate this actual source execution to the complete formula. The same contract requires typed_total, deterministic, input_preserved, no_external_io, no_floating_point, pure_data and restricted_runtime_only under normative Lean vscore-semantics/0.3 and data-pipeline/0.3.",
      "scope": ["all inputs satisfying A1", "actual canonical solve source and execution"],
      "dependencies": [
        {"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"},
        {"id": "A1", "relation": "assumes"}
      ],
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "For all integer n,m,a,b satisfying A1, the actual solve result equals Σ_{i=0}^{n-1} floor((a*i+b)/m).",
        "For every summand, floor division satisfies q*m <= a*i+b < (q+1)*m; truncation toward zero is insufficient.",
        "Every input with n=0 returns 0.",
        "solve({a:-2,b:1,m:3,n:4}) returns -4; solve({a:100,b:-99,m:7,n:0}) returns 0.",
        "The formal contract binds file program.vscore.json, entry solve, arity 1 and each of typed_total, deterministic, input_preserved, no_external_io, no_floating_point, pure_data and restricted_runtime_only.",
        "Universal source implementation refinement is required; examples, result existence or reflexive equalities cannot replace it."
      ],
